//? Title: Capsule Networks: Differentiable Routing and Explicit Margin/Decoder Fitting
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Vector capsules vote for output entities, route by agreement and squash their lengths.
We check routing against an independent oracle, verify the full MNIST network and decoder,
then expose every Adam update for margin, reconstruction and kernel regularization.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.5_attention_and_modern_convnets/capsule_networks.cpp`.

> The method

Squash maps a vector s to (norm²/(1+norm²))*s/sqrt(norm²+epsilon), with epsilon 1e-9 here.
It preserves direction; the familiar unregularized length norm²/(1+norm²) is approximate near
zero because of epsilon. Zero vectors and their first derivatives remain finite zero.
CapsuleLengths separately computes sqrt(sum(v²)+1e-9), giving a positive floor sqrt(1e-9).

For votes uhat_ij=W_ij*u_i, routing starts with b_ij=0 and repeats c=softmax_j(b),
s_j=sum_i(c_ij*uhat_ij), v_j=Squash(s_j), then b_ij+=dot(uhat_ij,v_j) except after the last
iteration. Couplings normalize over OUTPUT capsules. Every iteration stays in the tensor
graph, including agreement updates; no stop-gradient or optimizer is hidden in routing.
Its loop is forward computation, distinct from the explicit learned-parameter optimizer below.
The toy’s changing concentration is observed, not a universal monotonicity theorem.

The complete MNIST network uses VALID 9×9/256/ReLU (20×20), then 9×9/2/256 to form
6×6×32 primary eight-dimensional capsules (1152 total). Three routing iterations produce
ten 16D digit capsules. Vote weights start from N(0,.01), convolutions from He-uniform.
Log stabilized lengths serve as logits: softmax gives lengths normalized across classes,
which is a scoring convention, not a calibration guarantee. Without a decoder the model
has 6804224 learned scalars; with it 8215568. The decoder masks 160 digit coordinates, then
uses Glorot dense 512/ReLU,1024/ReLU and784/sigmoid. Its closure borrows the parameter store;
all decoder leaves exist before optimizer construction, and fresh graphs are built after updates.

$$L_{margin}=\mathrm{mean}_n\sum_k\left[T_k\max(0,.9-\ell_k)^2
+.5(1-T_k)\max(0,\ell_k-.1)^2\right].$$
\alttext(The present digit is pushed above length .9; absent digits are pushed below .1 with weight .5.)

Training minimizes this margin PLUS .0005 times mean summed-pixel reconstruction SSE and
.0001/2 times the sum of squared kernels. The decoder uses TRUE-class masks while fitting.
NLL of normalized lengths only monitors and selects validation checkpoints; the loop does
not silently replace margin fitting with cross entropy. Test reconstructions use PREDICTED
masks. Native Float64 finite differences verify gradients through routing inputs/vote weights,
and the full-model probe checks every parameter derivative with and without the decoder.

The visible run retains all capsules, widths, three routing iterations and decoder layers.
It uses 64 fit/32 validation/32 official-test original MNIST images, five batch-eight epochs,
Adam(.001), no augmentation and the explicit L2/reconstruction terms above. All preprocessing,
model, losses and updates use tensor operations; host arrays appear only in the independent
small routing oracle and plots. This bounded single-seed fit does not reproduce the paper's
all-data training, shift augmentation, overlapping-digit results or reported MNIST error.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/capsule_networks_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/capsule_networks_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/capsule_networks_concept.tikz > build/capsule_networks_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/capsule_networks_concept.svg build/capsule_networks_concept.dvi > build/capsule_networks_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
