// result_end
\caption(The visible optimizer minimizes margin plus .0005 times summed-pixel reconstruction and explicit kernel L2. Normalized-length NLL only monitors and selects checkpoints. The four panels show NLL, optimized data terms, 32 held-out predictions and mean test capsule lengths; the latter are not calibrated class probabilities.)
\alttext(The visible optimizer minimizes margin plus .0005 times summed-pixel reconstruction and explicit kernel L2. Normalized-length NLL only monitors and selects checkpoints. The four panels show NLL, optimized data terms, 32 held-out predictions and mean test capsule lengths; the latter are not calibrated class probabilities.)

> Selected decoder behavior

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/capsule_networks_reconstructions.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::set_num_threads(2);

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";
  dm::datasets::fetch("mnist", (cache / "mnist").string());

  const auto data = n::load_mnist((cache / "mnist").string(), "test");
  std::vector<int64_t> rows;
  for (int digit = 0; digit < 10; ++digit) {
    bool found = false;
    for (int row = 0; row < 64; ++row)
      if (data.labels.at({row}) == digit) {
        rows.push_back(row);
        found = true;
        break;
      }
    if (!found)
      return 1;
  }
  const auto images = n::take_rows(data.images, rows);
  n::NoGradGuard guard;
  n::ParameterStore p(17);
  n::models::CapsNet(p, n::zeros({1, 28, 28, 1}), 3, true);
  p.load("build/capsule_networks_best_params.npz");
  const auto out = n::models::CapsNet(p, images, 3, true);
  const auto reconstructed =
      out.reconstruct(n::one_hot(n::argmax(out.logits, 1), 10)).reshape({10, 28, 28, 1});
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(n::concat({images, reconstructed}, 0),
                     "build/capsule_networks_reconstructions.png", 5, 0., 1., 4, 1., 4);
  std::print("Top two rows: real test digits in class order0-9. Bottom two: "
             "selected-checkpoint reconstructions masked by PREDICTED class, not true labels. "
             "Unclear or wrong reconstructions remain visible.\n");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Top two rows: real test digits in class order0-9. Bottom two: selected-checkpoint reconstructions masked by PREDICTED class, not true labels. Unclear or wrong reconstructions remain visible.
\image(figures/capsule_networks_reconstructions.png)
// result_end
\caption(Top two rows show original official-test digits 0–4 then 5–9. Bottom two show the selected model’s decoder output for the same inputs, using predicted-class masks. Training used true-class masks; this visualization avoids true-label access in reconstruction and does not imply that every digit is recognized.)
\alttext(Top two rows show original official-test digits 0–4 then 5–9. Bottom two show the selected model’s decoder output for the same inputs, using predicted-class masks. Training used true-class masks; this visualization avoids true-label access in reconstruction and does not imply that every digit is recognized.)


> Observed subset result

Validation selected epoch 5, the last of the five, so this 40-update run ended before
validation NLL stopped improving: validation NLL 1.166203, inference fit NLL 0.947312,
test NLL 1.491150 and 24/32 correct test predictions (75%). Test margin is 0.259784
and mean predicted-mask reconstruction SSE is 53.478485 per image.
The decoder gallery remains blurry and similar across inputs. The short fit does not reproduce paper accuracy or high-quality reconstruction.

> Native confusion matrices

These matrices use the held-out predictions from the executed program above.
The native `ConfusionMatrix` SVG API labels exact counts with true classes
running from top to bottom and predicted classes from left to right.

\image(figures/capsule_networks_confusion_api_0.svg)
\caption(Held-out classification confusion counts, evaluation 1. Exact cell counts are printed in the image.)
\alttext(Integer prediction counts with true classes as rows and predicted classes as columns.)


> Conclusion

Differentiable agreement routing preserves the vector structure while an explicit outer
optimizer learns every filter, vote matrix and decoder layer. Component-wise loss traces,
held-out scoring and predicted-mask reconstructions expose what the bounded complete model
actually learned without treating lengths as calibrated probabilities or claiming paper accuracy.

> References

- [Sabour, Frosst and Hinton (2017), Dynamic Routing Between Capsules](https://arxiv.org/abs/1710.09829).
- [MNIST dataset](https://yann.lecun.org/exdb/mnist/).
